<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">readiness</ansi>

Your companions keep their condition, just as you do. A companion who
ends a fight on 8 of 60 health is still on 8 when you next log in.
Nothing refills them for free: not logging out, not a server restart, not
a level.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What they keep</ansi>

  Health and mana, lasting wounds (<ansi fg="command">help wounds</ansi>), level, and gear all
  carry over when you log out and back in, and across a server restart.
  If the server crashes, they come back as they were at the last
  automatic save, up to about a quarter of an hour before. Light wounds
  and the effects of a fight end with it.

  A companion who earns a level keeps the health and mana it had. A
  higher maximum just gives it more room to recover into. When it next
  comes back (a login, a restart), its health is held to its maximum and
  its wound limit, so health above a new wound's limit is lost then. A
  living companion never comes back below 1 health.

  A companion you had before this rule came in starts full once, then
  keeps its condition from then on.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How they recover</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">On the move.</ansi> Out of a fight, while you're logged in, companions regain
  health and mana just as you do: a little every few seconds, up to their
  wound limit. Nobody recovers while you're logged out, and no game time
  passes for it.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Healers and packs.</ansi> <ansi fg="command">heal wounds</ansi> spends your clerics' mana and your
  bandages and splints (<ansi fg="command">help heal</ansi>).

  <ansi fg="yellow">An inn.</ansi> A finished night at an inn knits every wound and restores you
  and every companion with you to full health and mana (<ansi fg="command">help inn</ansi>).

  <ansi fg="yellow">A camp.</ansi> A camp rest knits wounds with your splints and bandages, but
  doesn't restore health or mana itself: the company recovers on the
  move while it rests (<ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Death, flight, and separation</ansi>

  A companion raised by <ansi fg="command">resurrect</ansi> comes back with no wounds, at half its
  health and half its mana (<ansi fg="command">help resurrect</ansi>). One who fled a battle
  comes back as hurt as when it ran (<ansi fg="command">help morale</ansi>). One separated from
  you comes back as it left, without recovering while away
  (<ansi fg="command">help separation</ansi>).

<ansi fg="command">status</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">company status</ansi>, and <ansi fg="command">heal</ansi> show each member's health. See also:
<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>.
